    "body": "A compiled coroutine handles an exception and awaits a pure-Python coroutine. That coroutine suspends, then re-raises the same exception. When this happens, __Pyx_Coroutine_SendEx finds f_back already set on the top frame of the exception's traceback.\r\n\r\nThat top frame belongs to the finished Python coroutine. CPython set its f_back to the calling Python frame because the frame outlived its call (take_ownership() in Python/frame.c).\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: bwenstar <bwenstar@users.noreply.github.com>\r\n\r\nFixes #8042 \r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-16T19:07:38Z",
