                },
                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2026-10-13T21:12:44Z",
                    "email": "matusvalo@users.noreply.github.com",
                    "name": "Matus Valo"
                },
                "message": "Fix frame leak when an awaited Python coroutine re-raises the exception being handled\n\nA compiled coroutine handles an exception and awaits a pure-Python coroutine. That coroutine suspends, then re-raises the same exception. When this happens, __Pyx_Coroutine_SendEx finds f_back already set on the top frame of the exception's traceback.\n\nThat top frame belongs to the finished Python coroutine. CPython set its f_back to the calling Python frame because the frame outlived its call (take_ownership() in Python/frame.c).\n\nCo-authored-by: bwenstar <bwenstar@users.noreply.github.com>",
